  "text_md": "EXPLORER It had been interrupted because of the higher priority of the LHC cost overrun discussions. The Research Board agreed to restart this procedure starting with L3+C at the next Research Board.\n\nThe next meeting of the Research Board will take place on\n\nThursday,\n\n## ENCLOSURES\n\n- [1] Minutes of the 12th INTC meeting held on 13 2002 (INTC 2002-026/INTC 12) May\n- [2] Minutes of the 58th LHCC meeting held on 15-16 2002 (LHCC 2002-019/LHCC 58) May\n- [3] Minutes of the 58t SPSC meeting held on 21 2002 (SPSC 2002-022/SPSC 58) May\n\n## REFERENCES\n\n- [1] Minutes of the meeting of the Research Board held on 11 March 2002 (CERNIDGIRB 2001-332, MI57) 157t\n2. 2] Minutes of the meeting of the Research Board held on 11 April 2002 (CERNIDGIRB 2001-335, MI58) 158t\n3. 3] Neutron Cross Sections for the Pb Isotopes Implications for ADS and Nucleosynthesis (INTC 2001-020/P142)\n- [4] Measurements of fission cross sections for the isotopes relevant to the Thorium fuel (INTC 2001-025/P145) cycle\n5. 231 [5] Measurement of the neutron capture cross sections of and (INTC 2002-013/P154) 232 Th, 234U 236U; Pa,\n- [6] An Energy Upgrade of REX-Isolde to 3.1 MeVlu and Acceleration of Heavier Masses up to A=I50 (INTC 2002-009/P152)\n- [7] Fusion Reactions at the Coulomb Barrier with Neutron-rich Mg Isotopes (INTC 2002014/P155)\n8. 8] Evolution of single particle and collective properties in the neutron-rich Mg isotopes (INTC 2002-020/P159)\n9. [ 9] Summary, plan and resources of RD39 projects (LHCC 2002-015, Status Reportl RD39 1)\n- [10] Development of radiation hard semiconductor devices for very high luminosity colliders (LHCC 2002-003/P6)\n- [11] Status Report on the NA6O Pixel Detector Project (SPSC 2002-024/M689)\n- [12] Status Report of the HARP experiment (SPSC 2002-019/M685)\n- [13] Future plans; The DIRAC Collaboration (SPSC 2002-018/M684)",
